Source\n- Constructors:\n  - public JavaUtilRandomSource(long seed): deterministic for a given seed.\n- Methods:\n  - public int nextInt(int bound): delegates to java.util.Random, validating bound > 0; throws IllegalArgumentException if bound <= 0.\n\nMoveOutcome (src/main/java/MoveOutcome.java)\n- public enum MoveOutcome { MOVED, ATE_FOOD, GAME_OVER }\n- Semantics: result classification for a single tick.\n\nSnake (src/main/java/Snake.java)\n- public final class Snake\n- Constructors:\n  - public Snake(Position start): creates a snake with a single-segment body at start.\n- Methods:\n  - public Position head(): returns current head position.\n  - public Position tail(): returns current tail position.\n  - public int length(): number of segments.\n  - public boolean occupies(Position p): true if any segment equals p.\n  - public void moveTo(Position nextHead): adds nextHead at head and removes the last tail segment.\n  - public void growTo(Position nextHead): adds nextHead at head and retains tail (length+1).\n  - public java.util.List<Position> bodyAsList(): returns a defensive immutable/copy list of body positions in head-to-tail order.\n- Errors: Public methods validate non-null inputs and throw NullPointerException or IllegalArgumentException as appropriate.\n\nGameSnapshot (src/main/java/GameSnapshot.java)\n- public final class GameSnapshot\n- Constructors:\n  - public GameSnapshot(int width, int height, java.util.List<Position> body, Position food, int score, boolean gameOver, Direction direction)\n- Methods:\n  - public int getWidth()\n  - public int getHeight()\n  - public java.util.List<Position> getSnakeBody(): returns an unmodifiable copy/view.\n  - public Position getFood()\n  - public int getScore()\n  - public boolean isGameOver()\n  - public Direction getDirection()\n  - public String toString(): concise summary for debugging/logging.\n- Semantics: immutable snapshot suitable for observers/tests; must not reflect future state changes.\n\nSnakeGame (src/main/java/SnakeGame.java)\n- public final class SnakeGame\n- Constructors:\n  - public SnakeGame(int width, int height, RandomSource rng): initializes a new game with the snake at a valid starting cell, score=0, gameOver=false, initial direction (implementation-defined but consistent), and a randomly placed food on a free cell using rng.\n- Methods:\n  - public void reset(): resets to a fresh game state using the same width, height, and rng; places food randomly.\n  - public boolean setDirection(Direction dir): sets intended movement direction if dir is non-null and not an immediate reversal of current direction; returns true if accepted, false if rejected.\n  - public Direction getDirection(): current movement direction.\n  - public MoveOutcome tick(): advances exactly one cell by current direction. If next head is food, grows snake, increments score by 1, places new food randomly among free cells; returns ATE_FOOD. If next head is out-of-bounds or collides with the body, sets gameOver=true and returns GAME_OVER. Otherwise moves normally and returns MOVED. If the board is full after eating (no free cells), sets gameOver=true.\n  - public boolean isGameOver()\n  - public int getScore()\n  - public int getWidth()\n  - public int getHeight()\n  - public GameSnapshot snapshot(): returns an immutable snapshot of current state.\n  - public void placeFoodAt(Position p): deterministically place food at p after validating bounds and that p is not occupied by the snake; useful for tests.\n- Helper (non-public) methods:\n  - private void placeFoodRandomly(): choose uniformly among free cells using rng.nextInt(bound) where bound equals count of free cells.\n  - private boolean inBounds(Position p): 0 <= x < width and 0 <= y < height.\n- Errors: Constructor and reset validate width>0 and height>0; throw IllegalArgumentException otherwise. placeFoodAt throws IllegalArgumentException for out-of-bounds or occupied cells. tick on gameOver leaves state unchanged and returns GAME_OVER.\n- Grid: origin top-left; x increases to the right, y increases downward.\n\nMain (src/main/java/Main.java)\n- public final class Main\n- Methods:\n  - public static void main(String[] args): creates JavaUtilRandomSource with a fixed seed, constructs SnakeGame with a small grid, prints initial snapshot, performs a few deterministic ticks printing MoveOutcome and final snapshot, catches any Exception by printing a single line and exiting normally (no rethrow).\n\nImport direction rules\n- Core domain (Position, Direction, MoveOutcome, Snake, GameSnapshot, SnakeGame, RandomSource) must not import environment-dependent classes.\n- Environment-dependent (Main, JavaUtilRandomSource) may depend on core domain.\n- Tests import and exercise only the canonical API and may define in-test stubs for RandomSource.\n",
    "Shared Knowledge": "Project is a Maven Java 11 application. Core domain logic is separated from environment/runtime. Randomness is abstracted via RandomSource; JavaUtilRandomSource is the only environment adapter. SnakeGame orchestrates rules and exposes a stable API. GameSnapshot provides read-only state for tests/observers. Main is a minimal, non-interactive demo. Tests are headless, deterministic, and live in src/test/java/MainTest.java, validating runtime wiring and representative rules without GUI or I/O.",
